{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>On this very day.</b> Since the day of a person's death is called his sun's setting, and Moses at his death — his eye did not dim nor his moisture flee, therefore he appeared as though he were still standing in the middle of his days, that is, 'on this very day' — when the sun is at its full strength."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:16:09.288911992Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}